     MicroHost is designed to be a file-transfer system with a few extras.
     The upload and download functions use standard XMODEM (not CRC). If
     you have difficulty, make certain you are using XMODEM.

     To page the SYSOP for a chat, enter C at the prompt. This puts a
     notice on his or her screen that you have asked for a chat. If
     available, they will break in and respond. It isn't necessary to
     enter CHAT more than once.

     Enter your name the same way every time you call. If you don't,
     any mail you may have waiting won't be found. Mail is delivered
     automatically when you first log on. You can send mail to the
     SYSOP by entering E at the prompt. NOTE that only one message is
     stored at a time; if you enter another before the first has been
     read, the first message will be erased.

     The Bulletin file can be read by entering B at the prompt.

     Log off by entering G at the prompt. Don't just hang up in mid-call.

     If there are blank lines between every line you see, set your end of
     line character to CR only, not CR + LF.

